Module hume "Half the Hive" {
  // ── The account ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // At eight on the evening of the Turning-out, to a company anywhere in the Wold (or when it next comes into it): each
  // strand's morning after, plainly; then one ending, by where the Mother went. The world goes on after.
  Query accounting() means flightDay() and (hour(clock) >= 20 or day(clock) >= leftDay(hume_wold) + 3).

  // You.
  Rule fate_forced within hume_wold when accounting() and forcedSwarm(party) and not spread(fate_you) says "You chose for the bees. The Searchers know it; the Sisters do not, and never will. Kestrel Dunn has not said your name since, and will not, either to curse it or to thank you." { Assert spread(fate_you). }
  Rule fate_hannet_broken within hume_wold when accounting() and failedHannet(party) and not spread(fate_you) says "Hannet Coke is sitting on the slope of the empty Dancing Hall where the marks of this week's dances are newest, with two wax bees on a cord round her neck. She does not blame you. She says so, to anyone who asks, which is worse." { Assert spread(fate_you). }
  Rule fate_named within hume_wold when accounting() and named(party) and not spread(fate_you) says "You are of the Comb now. The scent will not come off: you will smell, a little, of the Mother for the rest of your life, in the lowland, in the rain, in your grave; and any Sister anywhere in the Wold will turn her head toward you, and away, as if you were family." { Assert spread(fate_you). }
  Entity fate_you: fact "you".
  // The lovers, and the Stair.
  Rule fate_lovers_gone within hume_wold when accounting() and goes(linnet) and goes(eben) and stairLit(eben) and not spread(fate_lovers) says "Linnet Amory keeps the old Mother in the new comb, and Eben Candlish is carving the doorframe of the first cell, and at midsummer, in the Brow they left, the sun comes down the Lantern Stair from the Crown to the Brood like water down a drain, and people come from Sallowcomb and Ketter to stand at the foot of it." { Assert spread(fate_lovers). }
  Rule fate_lovers_gone_short within hume_wold when accounting() and goes(linnet) and goes(eben) and not spread(fate_lovers) says "Linnet Amory keeps the old Mother in the new comb, and Eben Candlish is carving the doorframe of the first cell. In the Brow, the Lantern Stair goes up three turns and stops at nothing, and the children of the Waxwrights dare each other to climb to the last step and stand on it." { Assert spread(fate_lovers). }
  Rule fate_lovers_home within hume_wold when accounting() and not goes(linnet) and not goes(eben) and not spread(fate_lovers) says "Linnet Amory and Eben Candlish stayed, both of them, and are to be married at the Feast of the Lime, and Eben is finishing the Stair, slowly, now there is no hurry; and somewhere across the Wold a boy of seventeen is keeping the old Mother in a new comb, and writing back every week to ask how to do it." { Assert spread(fate_lovers). }
  Rule fate_lovers_crossed within hume_wold when accounting() and goes(eben) and not goes(linnet) and not spread(fate_lovers) says "Eben Candlish walked out after the bees without a word to anyone, and is in the new comb, carving nothing; and Linnet Amory, who stayed for him so that he could finish the Stair, keeps the Daughters in the Brow, and goes every evening to the Waxwrights' gallery and stands at the foot of the Lantern Stair, three turns up and stopping at nothing, and nobody has had the heart yet to tell her he meant to do the same for her." { Assert spread(fate_lovers). }
  Entity fate_lovers: fact "the lovers".
  // Hannet.
  Rule fate_hannet_carried within hume_wold when accounting() and goes(hannet) and not left(gallowtree) and not spread(fate_hannet) says "Hannet Coke went with the Mother at last, carried, complaining the whole way, and sits now in the sun at the mouth of the new comb on a stool somebody made her, telling the children how it was done in the old Brow, mostly wrongly, with two wax bees on a cord round her neck." { Assert spread(fate_hannet). }
  Rule fate_hannet_tree within hume_wold when accounting() and goes(hannet) and left(gallowtree) and not spread(fate_hannet) says "Hannet Coke went with the Mother at last, two hours, on her own legs, to the Gallowtree, and sits on the knoll in the sun, happy, and does not know whose tree it is." { Assert spread(fate_hannet). }
  Rule fate_hannet_home within hume_wold when accounting() and not goes(hannet) and not failedHannet(party) and not spread(fate_hannet) says "Hannet Coke stayed, for the seventh time. She sits on the slope of the empty Dancing Hall in the afternoons and runs, very short, very slow, the line of a dance for somewhere, to nobody." { Assert spread(fate_hannet). }
  Entity fate_hannet: fact "Hannet".
  // Agnes, Tobit, and the thing in the dark.
  Rule fate_agnes_carried within hume_wold when accounting() and goes(agnes) and linnetPermitsDead(linnet) and not spread(fate_agnes) says "Agnes Mellor carried her husband out of the Brow on a litter, capped, by leave of the keeper, the first of the dead ever to go with a Leaving; and he stands now in the first wall of the new comb, alone in it, with a view." { Assert spread(fate_agnes). }
  Rule fate_agnes_likeness within hume_wold when accounting() and goes(agnes) and likenessGiven(agnes) and not spread(fate_agnes) says "Agnes Mellor went with the Mother with a little wax Tobit wrapped in her shawl, his head on one side the way he stood when he was waiting for her to stop talking; and she stops talking, sometimes, now, and waits." { Assert spread(fate_agnes). }
  Rule fate_agnes_freed within hume_wold when accounting() and goes(agnes) and not spread(fate_agnes) says "Agnes Mellor went with the Mother, and left Tobit capped in the Gallery with the others, safe, and has a view." { Assert spread(fate_agnes). }
  Rule fate_agnes_stays within hume_wold when accounting() and not goes(agnes) and not spread(fate_agnes) says "Agnes Mellor stayed. She sits in the Capped Gallery every night in the dark with Tobit, on her stool, talking about the goat." { Assert spread(fate_agnes). }
  Entity fate_agnes: fact "Agnes".
  Rule fate_moth_dead within hume_wold when accounting() and mothDead(deathshead) and not spread(fate_moth) says "Nothing comes into the Capped Gallery in the small hours now." { Assert spread(fate_moth). }
  Rule fate_moth_alive within hume_wold when accounting() and not mothDead(deathshead) and not spread(fate_moth) says "Something still comes into the Capped Gallery in the small hours, soft and dry, smelling of the Mother, and drinks from the seals of the dead; and the children of the Brow have a name for it, and a rhyme, and will not go up the honey stair after dark." { Assert spread(fate_moth). }
  Entity fate_moth: fact "the Gallery".
  // Nell, and the squire.
  Rule fate_nell_named within hume_wold when accounting() and nellNamed(nell) and not spread(fate_nell) says "Nell Quarrie goes up the stair in the afternoons now, in daylight, scented by Elspet Garnock's own hand, and sits with Aldo, fourth row on the left, with the light coming down the arch; and has shut her shop, because she finds she has no more use for the oil." { Assert spread(fate_nell). }
  Rule fate_nell_barred within hume_wold when accounting() and nellBarred(nell) and not spread(fate_nell) says "Nell Quarrie's shop in Smoke End has a mark on the door that the Comb reads, and she does not go up the gorge, and in the evenings she stands at the foot of the path with her eyes shut, smelling." { Assert spread(fate_nell). }
  Rule fate_nell_none within hume_wold when accounting() and not spread(fate_nell) says "Once a month Nell Quarrie goes up the stair in the dark smelling of her own oil, and sits an hour with Aldo, and comes down, and nobody notices." { Assert spread(fate_nell). }
  Entity fate_nell: fact "Nell".
  Rule fate_corve_gift within hume_wold when accounting() and corveGives(corve) and not spread(fate_corve) says "Squire Lucian Corve of Larkhill is of the Comb, named by the keeper's own hand, and goes up the stair in the Brow every week with his drawing-board, and has redrawn the Mother twice, and is still getting her wrong, and does not mind." { Assert spread(fate_corve). }
  Rule fate_corve_robbed within hume_wold when accounting() and flaskGone(corve) and not flaskAt(larkhill) and not corveGives(corve) and not spread(fate_corve) says "Squire Corve's oak case is empty, and he has not said a word to anyone about it, because he cannot. He writes to the keeper this spring as every spring, and asks, as every spring, to be named; and does not mention the flask; and nor does the keeper." { Assert spread(fate_corve). }
  Rule fate_corve_none within hume_wold when accounting() and not left(larkhill) and not spread(fate_corve) says "At Larkhill the squire's tower stands empty and dry and pointed, with an empty green flask in a crack at the top of it; and the squire sits in his study among twelve years of drawings and does not draw." { Assert spread(fate_corve). }
  Entity fate_corve: fact "Corve".
  // Moss, the Daughters, Ivo, the mead, the Drewes.
  Rule fate_moss_hurt within hume_wold when accounting() and mossHurt(moss) and not spread(fate_moss) says "Moss Ashdown can walk again, with a stick. The Leaving went without him." { Assert spread(fate_moss). }
  Rule fate_moss_brocks within hume_wold when accounting() and brocksKilled(brocks) and not mossHurt(moss) and not spread(fate_moss) says "Moss Ashdown has two brock claws on a thong round his neck and a song in every comb in the Wold, and does not sing it, and does not wear the claws when Kestrel is near." { Assert spread(fate_moss). }
  Entity fate_moss: fact "Moss".
  Rule fate_daughters_pierced within hume_wold when accounting() and breckPierced(brenna) and not spread(fate_daughters) says "The Candlish princess reigns in the Brow, and the Candlishes are the Mother's household for thirty years, and do not know what to do with it. Dame Brenna Breck has not left her cell in the Brood since the night, and her grandson Tibby brings her meals, with his drone, and she eats them." { Assert spread(fate_daughters). }
  Rule fate_daughters_cast within hume_wold when accounting() and castWent(brenna) and not spread(fate_daughters) says "The Breck princess reigns in the Brow; and the princess who was caged went out with a cast the next noon, south, with forty people behind her, toward somewhere nobody danced for; and no word has come back yet. The Comb has never had two Leavings in one summer. Some say it is against nature. Some say Garnock would have been proud." { Assert spread(fate_daughters). }
  Rule fate_daughters_shamed within hume_wold when accounting() and brennaShamed(brenna) and not spread(fate_daughters) says "The Breck princess woke first, as she was always going to, fed with a spoon, and stung her sisters in their cells, and reigns; and Dame Brenna Breck is the Mother's household for thirty years, and walks through the Brood upright in black with a silver bee at her throat, and finds that she is looked at, now, in another way, and that it is not the way she wanted." { Assert spread(fate_daughters). }
  Rule fate_daughters_none within hume_wold when accounting() and not spread(fate_daughters) says "The Breck princess woke first and stung her sisters in their cells, and reigns, and the Brecks are the Mother's household at last after a hundred years, and everyone says what a strong queen she is, and how lucky." { Assert spread(fate_daughters). }
  Entity fate_daughters: fact "the Daughters".
  Rule fate_ivo_founder within hume_wold when accounting() and goes(ivo) and not spread(fate_ivo) says "Ivo Gildersleeve is a Searcher of the new comb, in a yellow coat gone brown with walking, and has been out every day since they came, finding things: water, wild comb, a quicker way, a better view. Kestrel Dunn has told him twice to stop showing off, and once, when she thought nobody could hear, that he was the best she ever trained, which is untrue, because she never trained him." { Assert spread(fate_ivo). }
  Rule fate_ivo_with within hume_wold when accounting() and travelsWith(ivo, party) and not spread(fate_ivo) says "Ivo Gildersleeve is with you, in a yellow coat gone brown with walking, and knows the way." { Assert spread(fate_ivo). }
  Rule fate_ivo_out within hume_wold when accounting() and ivoTurnedOut(ivo) and not spread(fate_ivo) says "Ivo Gildersleeve was turned out with the Escort, with a cloak and a loaf, and is sitting on a milestone at the edge of the Wold looking down the drove road at the lowland, which he has never seen, deciding." { Assert spread(fate_ivo). }
  Rule fate_ivo_kept within hume_wold when accounting() and ivoSearcher(ivo) and not spread(fate_ivo) says "Ivo Gildersleeve was not turned out. He is a Searcher of the Brow, the first of the Escort ever to be one, and the Escort do not know whether to be proud of him." { Assert spread(fate_ivo). }
  Entity fate_ivo: fact "Ivo".
  Rule fate_mead within hume_wold when accounting() and meadSaved(huw) and not spread(fate_mead) says "A cask of Huw Penry's last mead is laid down in the honey vaults of the Brow to be broached at every Calling for thirty years, chalked PENRY · THE YEAR HE WENT, and Martin Sayle in Smoke End says it is the second-best mead in the Wold, and will not say which is the first." { Assert spread(fate_mead). }
  Entity fate_mead: fact "the mead".
  Rule fate_drewes within hume_wold when accounting() and drewesPaid(party) and not spread(fate_drewes) says "The Drewes bought a goat with what you paid them, at the last farm before the moor, and walked it all the way, and it is the only goat in the new comb, and the younger girl has named it after you." { Assert spread(fate_drewes). }
  Entity fate_drewes: fact "the Drewes".

  // ── Endings ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Query told() means spread(fate_daughters) and spread(fate_ivo) and spread(fate_nell).
  Ending far_free "Under the Far Brow" when accounting() and told() and left(far_brow) and kestrelTurned(kestrel) "Under the Far Brow the new comb hangs a yard long already, white going gold, and the old came by the shepherds' drove and are there to see it. It is the best place in the Wold, as Kestrel always said; and this time everyone could walk it. There are child-handprints at the back in the old wax, and new ones beside them now, and one that a grown man says is his from when he was nine, and nobody knows whose the oldest are, or why the first comb here was ever left. Half the hive went. Half stayed. Both halves are alive.".
  Ending far_hard "The Long Way" when accounting() and told() and left(far_brow) "Under the Far Brow the new comb hangs a yard long, white going gold, in the best place in the Wold, as Kestrel always said. The young are there, and the strong. The old stayed home, mostly, knowing they could not walk it, and some who tried did not come in, and the Leaving goes on without them. Kestrel Dunn was right about the place. She was wrong about who could walk it. She knows.".
  Ending dell_peace "The Brocks' Peace" when accounting() and told() and left(chalk_dell) and brockTruce(brocks) "In the Chalk Dell the new comb fills the cave in the chalk, and the brocks sleep in a smaller hole at the back and are given the old comb at the turn of the year, as the marks say, and keep the peace. Moss Ashdown is cutting new marks under the old ones, for whoever comes next, so that this time somebody reads them.".
  Ending dell_blood "The Dell" when accounting() and told() and left(chalk_dell) and brocksKilled(brocks) "In the Chalk Dell the new comb fills the cave where the brocks lived, and it is dry and warm and faces south and is the best-sheltered comb in the Wold; and at the back of the Dell the chalk is stained, and the children are told not to go there, and do.".
  Ending dell_raided "The Brocks' Cave" when accounting() and told() and left(chalk_dell) "The brocks came back for their cave the first night, and every night after. The Leaving holds the Dell, just; the comb is in the cave and the brocks are in the dark at the back of the Dell, and every night the Searchers sit up with torches, and every morning someone counts. It is a good place. It is going to cost.".
  Ending lark_gift "The Gift at Larkhill" when accounting() and told() and left(larkhill) and corveGives(corve) "The chantry tower at Larkhill hums like a struck bell from dawn to dusk, and belongs to nobody, by a deed of gift in a neat hand that the Wold has framed. The lowland markets are a morning's walk away. The squire comes up from the farmhouse every evening and sits in the yard with his drawing-board, scented, and the Sisters walk across his paper.".
  Ending lark_owned "The Squire's Bees" when accounting() and told() and left(larkhill) "The Leaving lives in the chantry tower at Larkhill, safe and dry and a morning from market; and the bees, and the comb, and the honey, are the property of L. Corve, Esquire, by the law of the lowland, which the Humefolk have never had to know before and are learning. He has not taken a single pot. He has not been in among them. He cannot bring himself to, and they cannot bring themselves to ask him.".
  Ending gallow "The Eighth Leaving" when accounting() and told() and left(gallowtree) "In the Gallowtree the new comb grows white over the grey, up the inside of the old tree, over the faces of the seventh Leaving, whom the eighth have decided not to speak about. The tree is green and loud with bees. It is wet at the heart. It will be a long winter, and when the Searchers of the Brow walk out to the knoll at the thaw to see how the eighth Leaving did, they will find out, as the Brow has always said of the seventh, whether they went on east.".
  Ending bivouac "In the Open" when accounting() and told() and left(high_wold) "The swarm hangs on the honey linden in the open air, building white comb in the wind and the sun, and the Leaving camps under it, and waits for the bees to change their minds, which bees do not. It is a fine summer. Nobody talks about the winter.".
}
